  "desc": "A chunky, persistent-canvas Lissajous curve morphs continuously between integer frequency pairs. Six hundred grid-snapped samples leave a restrained phosphor trail while the phase advances forever.",
  "seen": "Seen on: mona_biasia's Lissajous SVG generator, datacurve icon sets, vector oscilloscopes, and pixel instrument panels",
  "hint": "drag either stepped frequency slider; use its native arrow, Page, Home, and End keys; press R to reset",
  "prompt": "Build Pixel Lissajous from the exact 147 supplied 5×5 SVG pixels and four 3px frequency bars. Preserve the illustrated first-pose lengths of 70/42/70/28px at their captured positions. Project all 600 original sine samples into the compact grid and retain the complete persistent trail, moving phase, original 800ms interrupted frequency model, defaults a=3/b=4 and both native 1–9 ranges. Live range fills reflect those original parameter values. Full retains the original complete 360×196 field and readable parameter controls. Expose Reset in the shell and preserve R reset and native range keys. Keep the documented sparse-fill exception without enlarging supplied geometry. Use the v4 neutral palette and self-hosted Geist/Geist Mono. Keep a 240×168 hero plane with exact native artwork and a separate complete 400×400 full composition with a readable scroll camera. Prefix every class with rootClass. Keep controls in the shell, support native keys and touch scrolling, preserve source timing and datasets, freeze work during independent caller/viewport holds, and clean up frames, observers, capture and font/image work. Reduced motion keeps an intentional still with interruptible 150ms opacity feedback. Portable exports resolve both fonts and licensed assets without network access.\n\nKeep native vertical page scrolling available when the full viewport reaches its bounds, while retaining horizontal overscroll containment, deliberate camera panning and the original geometry, assets and complete model.",
